                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As a longtime horror fan, I watched a gameplay of Dreadout back when it came out and I remember I enjoyed it, so of course I had to play it myself, especially now that the third game is a work in progress, but I was left pretty disappointed honestly.\r\n\r\nI'm a huge Fatal Frame fan, and I don't find Dreadout a \"rightful successor\" nor a game that should be compared to FF, the only similarity is the camera, but we're given no real explanation as to why Linda's camera can exorcise ghosts or anything of she sort, and in general I find the lore to be lacking. The first act of the game offers no explanation at all past \"Oh yeah we're looking for our friend\", the puzzles aren't enjoyable and you can only meet 5 or so ghosts, none of them being memorable in the slightest imo.\r\n\r\nThe second act is somehow even less linear, you're thrown into new areas without even a little explanation and everything is so vague that it's impossible to understand what's going on without looking up explanations/theories, and the enemies here are memorable design-wise but that's it, I enjoyed one of the fights a lot and also the maze bit, but I find the endings, the gameplay and pretty much everything to be underwhelming and disappointed.\r\n\r\nThe game was gifted to me during a sale, but it's just not worth it, the gameplay is clunky, the mc has no spoken lines and not much of a personality and the other characters are absent through most of the game. I was very hyped for the ghost's stories, but they're disappointing too, there's only two ghosts that are somehow interesting, but one of them doesn't even appear unless you collect the right items, and even then she doesn't do much. I'm sure the game is more enjoyable to those who know the folklore well, but to me it was just so underwhelming, I wouldn't even replay to get the achievements (for now), I hope the third game will be so much better.\r\n\r\nI also expected more from the dlc manga, but it's just like the rest of the game, lots of things happening but nothing clearly explained, to the point I wonder what was even the point of it? just to show that other people were lured there? I would've preferred something focused on Ira and Linda, or literally anything with more relevant lore. Overall, I'd say this game is a 5/10.",
